the green knight seems just about as  far-fetched as a movie can be  fortunately it's also one of the most  interesting upcoming big screen  offerings out there  its first trailer has dropped and it  makes clear that fans are right to  expect great things  let's take a moment to break it down the  teaser opens with the knights of the  round table in camelot and their ruler  king arthur requests entertainment for  himself and his queen in a textbook case  of be careful what you ask for  a monstrous green knight who looks like  he's made out of wood steps in  and challenges a knight to take a free  shot at him the young sir gawain played  by dev patel  is quick to accept the challenge and  decapitates the strange visitor it's at  this point that the green knight picks  up his head and proclaims  one yeah hence  as the rest of the trailer makes clear  this means gawain must meet the monster  in a year to complete the game and  receive a blow in turn  it's pretty clear that the green knight  enters the castle with full knowledge  that he was setting his opponent up not  least because he delivers a  pitch-perfect evil laugh as he flees in  full headless horseman mode while gawain  might be concerned with the fact that  his days are numbered the trailer makes  sure that the viewer can't help but  wonder exactly what the green knight is  all about the year has almost passed and  gawain seems intent on setting the whole  green knight incident aside however his  king doesn't want to hear any of it in a  meeting between gawain and arthur the  ruler states in fairly clear terms that  gowan must find the green knight to  fulfill his pact and just like that a  quest is given  because the green knight survived  gawain's blow and the mythical king of  britons turns out to be a completionist  the young knight has no choice but to  leave the confines of arthur's  stronghold and travel through a land  that's unlike anything he's seen before  it's a solid and ominous start for an  epic adventure  as sir gawain rides toward an  unfortunate fate a creepy voice  speaks ill of his chances for survival  it's easy to assume that the raspy  whisper belongs to a soothsayer  or witch of some sort but the source of  these pessimistic predictions turns out  to be an otherwise perfectly cute and  furry fox that for some reason chooses  to hang out with gawain it appears that  whatever fate awaits the young knight  the fox isn't particularly happy about  it  why do you stop me  since the very next thing we see is  gawain swinging his axe at the camera  and the shot looks a whole lot like it  might be from the fox's point of view  it's unclear if the fox is trying to  warn the knight of a threat or  making one either way a talking fox  seems like a pretty cool creature in the  movie's heavy fantasy setting  and we can only hope that it won't meet  its doom  the green knight is a pretty  star-studded production and the trailer  features all sorts of legendary  characters and amazing creatures even so  one of its most threatening figures  seems to be entirely human though not  any less dangerous for it right after  the fox has given its warnings and  gawain swings his axe the trailer  introduces the scavenger this character  is a bandit who manages to tie gawain up  and steal his massive weapon  the fact that the scavenger and his men  manage to defeat a knight of the round  table is one thing the fact that he  appears to be aware of gawain's quest  takes things to a completely different  level  sir gawain climbs a hill he observes a  misty vista  over which a group of gigantic shadowy  figures slowly march toward an  unknown destination gawain doesn't seem  awfully surprised or shocked to see them  and in the very next moment he lifts his  axe and appears to scream triumphantly  it creates the impression that gawain  has been actively seeking out these  giants or  at least knows what they are and is very  pleased to witness their travels in  person  eagle-eyed viewers will also note that  the fox from earlier seems to be by his  side  as such there's a chance that whatever  happens between the two in the forest  earlier in the trailer the fox survives  the meeting to annoy gawain even further  as befits the trailer's general air of  mystery the nature of the giants remains  very much up in the air though their  introductory shot shows them just  wandering  a later one shows one of them reaching  for gawain did the knight intend to seek  them out or did he just stumble in their  dangerous path  this remains to be seen  a casual viewing of the trailer might  give you the impression that it gives  away a whole lot of the plot of the  green knight however the moments near  the end make it clear that the trailer  only barely scratches the surface  the movie has plenty of big name actors  that we barely see in the trailer  for instance joel edgerton's lord alicia  vikander's lady  and aaron kellyman's winfred toward the  end of the trailer we see a succession  of quick adequately mysterious shots  featuring several of the hitherto unseen  characters  lord in particular gets a quick  shirtless scene and later returns to ask  awayne what he hopes to gain from his  mission gawain seems to have come  a long way from the opening moments of  the trailer since his answer is clear  and devoid of his earlier hesitancy he  declares that he does his work for honor  because that is why knight does what he  does  the trailer ends in pretty much the only  way it can as the last words of his  heroic reply to the lord linger we see  gawain enter some sort of wooded area in  which nature seems to have taken over  the green knight awaits within walking  down a set of stairs to meet gawain and  asks if the knight is ready  this fortunately isn't even close to a  spoiler though the trailer offers a  series of short exciting glimpses into  the movie's world  it does a commendable job at not  revealing anything beyond the most  general outline of the plot there are  still many entirely unexplained moments  such as the halo crown and the  inexplicable scene that features  gawain's head seemingly catching fire  all in all it seems that while the green  knight trailer gives glimpses of some of  the film secrets it has also hinted at  even greater and deeper ones that you  can't  possibly hope to comprehend without  seeing the movie that's the sign of a  pretty great trailer  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the green knight are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

